From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:46:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/22] DFlash2 drafter head on the INT4 records behind
 G6_DFL_HEAD_I4

G6_DFL_HEAD_I4=1 (default 0, needs --dflash-manifest): the DFlash2 drafter's
head GEMV binds the INT4 g32 records of the rank's vocab slice instead of the
target's MXFP8 records (dflash.cuh dfl_head_i4). It reuses the MTP draft's
copy when G6_DRAFT_HEAD_I4 made one (same slice, same G6_DRAFT_HEAD_KS pair
repack), else makes one the same way (rank.cuh head_i4_records, now shared by
both). In the S2 runtime signature. The target's head and the verify step
are unchanged.

In selector mode the head's raw logits pick each row's global top-16
(k_top_local) and enter the walk's scores (logit + pred . hp . succ).
Offline proxy on the MTP draft vectors (19,096 head inputs, E9 held-out):
target token in the top-16 97.00% MXFP8 vs 97.02% INT4 (paired +0.02 pt
[-0.05, +0.09]); top-16 overlap 96.1%; |dlogit| on the top-16 median 0.13,
p99 0.54.
